{"uid":"5183e1629ccad62d","name":"Team Name sorting toggles deterministically","fullName":"tests.e2e.admin.test_teams.TestTeams#test_team_name_sorting_toggles_deterministically","historyId":"d56dcbd1cfc0f9250e01d3ba09ad0634","time":{"start":1794547552192,"stop":1794547557531,"duration":5339},"description":"Objective: Team Name sorting toggles deterministically.\nPreconditions: Kesef CRM QA is available; the Teams listing contains at least two visible rows and the current account can view it.\nSteps:\n1. Log in with the configured automation account.\n2. Open Teams from the sidebar.\n3. Click the Team Name column header.\n4. Capture the visible Team Name values after loading settles.\n5. Click the Team Name column header again.\n6. Capture the visible Team Name values after loading settles.\n7. Verify each visible page is ordered consistently with its accessible sort direction and the second click reverses that direction.\nExpected: 1. Each click completes without a page/API error.\n2. The Team Name header exposes ascending or descending state.\n3. Visible values match the exposed direction after each click.\n4. The second click exposes the opposite direction; server-side pagination may legitimately return a different visible record page.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Objective: Team Name sorting toggles deterministically.<br />\nPreconditions: Kesef CRM QA is available; the Teams listing contains at least two visible rows and the current account can view it.<br />\nSteps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Log in with the configured automation account.</li>\n<li>Open Teams from the sidebar.</li>\n<li>Click the Team Name column header.</li>\n<li>Capture the visible Team Name values after loading settles.</li>\n<li>Click the Team Name column header again.</li>\n<li>Capture the visible Team Name values after loading settles.</li>\n<li>Verify each visible page is ordered consistently with its accessible sort direction and the second click reverses that direction.<br />\nExpected: 1. Each click co